## The bug: cleanup finds nothing

Both builds print `WARNING: The following filter keys were not present in any resource : labels.app, labels.managed-by`. I think instance templates have no resource-level labels. The `--labels` flag sets labels on the servers created from the template, under `properties.labels`. So my filter has never matched anything, and the empty cleanup output was not "fewer than 5 builds" as I said earlier. I was wrong. Images do carry resource labels from Packer, so the image side is fine.

Confirm it first:
```bash
gcloud compute instance-templates list --project=pg-ae-n-app-125609 --filter="properties.labels.managed-by=cloudbuild-packer" --format="table(name,selfLink.scope(projects))"
```
If it lists your recent pipeline templates, the corrected filter below is right.

**Replace the cleanup step in each `cloudbuild.yaml`** (backend shown, with the `cn-frontend` names for the frontend). It stays in dry-run, and it now prints how many templates it matched:
```yaml
  - id: Cleanup Old Packer Artifacts
    name: 'gcr.io/cloud-builders/gcloud'
    entrypoint: bash
    args:
      - -c
      - |
        # Deletes ONLY pipeline-created templates/images beyond the newest KEEP.
        # DRY_RUN=1 prints only. Set DRY_RUN=0 after reviewing a dry-run log.
        KEEP=5
        DRY_RUN=1
        PROJECT=pg-ae-n-app-125609
        IN_USE=$$(gcloud compute instance-groups managed describe cn-backend-mig-regional --region=me-central2 --project=$$PROJECT --format="value(versions[].instanceTemplate.basename())")
        ALL=$$(gcloud compute instance-templates list --project=$$PROJECT \
          --filter="properties.labels.managed-by=cloudbuild-packer AND properties.labels.app=cn-backend AND name~^cn-backend-template-[0-9a-f]{7}$$" \
          --sort-by=~creationTimestamp --format="value(name)")
        echo "matched pipeline templates: $$(echo "$$ALL" | grep -c .)"
        echo "$$ALL" | tail -n +$$((KEEP+1)) | while read T; do
          [ -z "$$T" ] && continue
          if echo "$$IN_USE" | grep -qw "$$T"; then echo "SKIP in use: $$T"; continue; fi
          SHA=$${T#cn-backend-template-}
          IMG=$$(gcloud compute images list --project=$$PROJECT --filter="name=cn-backend-image-$$SHA AND labels.managed-by=cloudbuild-packer" --format="value(name)")
          if [ "$$DRY_RUN" = "1" ]; then
            echo "DRY RUN would delete template $$T and image $${IMG:-none}"
          else
            gcloud compute instance-templates delete "$$T" --region=me-central2 --project=$$PROJECT --quiet
            if [ -n "$$IMG" ]; then gcloud compute images delete "$$IMG" --project=$$PROJECT --quiet; fi
          fi
        done
        exit 0
```
I haven't verified that `delete` accepts `--region` for regional templates. That matters only when you set `DRY_RUN=0`, so keep it at 1 until a dry run shows sensible names.

